WEBVTT

1
00:00:30.916 --> 00:00:35.041
<b>In the previous verses, Lord Krishna </b>
<b>described various types of sacrifices,</b>

2
00:00:35.041 --> 00:00:39.291
<b>and we also learned that sacrifice </b>
<b>does not only mean an altar,</b>

3
00:00:39.291 --> 00:00:43.500
<b>fire, and offering ghee and materials into it.</b>

4
00:00:43.500 --> 00:00:50.291
<b>Any selfless renunciation for one's spiritual </b>
<b>progress is akin to sacrifice.</b>

5
00:00:50.291 --> 00:00:56.458
<b>Now, here, Lord Krishna will reveal the </b>
<b>higher purpose hidden behind these sacrifices.</b>

6
00:01:01.375 --> 00:01:05.625
<b>In this verse, Lord Krishna presents </b>
<b>the essence of all sacrifices.</b>

7
00:01:05.625 --> 00:01:09.666
<b>He explains that regardless of the</b>
<b>form of the sacrifice —</b>

8
00:01:09.666 --> 00:01:15.666
<b>whether it is charity, austerity, the practice </b>
<b>of yoga, or the study of sacred texts —</b>

9
00:01:15.666 --> 00:01:18.458
<b>they all have the same ultimate goal:</b>

10
00:01:18.458 --> 00:01:24.541
<b>to purify oneself and move </b>
<b>towards spiritual progress.</b>

11
00:01:24.541 --> 00:01:27.791
<b>The learned who understand the true </b>
<b>significance of these sacrifices</b>

12
00:01:27.791 --> 00:01:32.666
<b>use them to cleanse the sins </b>
<b>accumulated through their actions.</b>

13
00:01:32.666 --> 00:01:36.541
<b>By participating in these sacrifices, </b>
<b>they purify themselves,</b>

14
00:01:36.541 --> 00:01:40.833
<b>and this purification is the first </b>
<b>result of these sacrifices.</b>

15
00:01:40.833 --> 00:01:46.375
<b>It is through the renunciation inherent in these </b>
<b>sacrifices that one learns to control their senses,</b>

16
00:01:46.375 --> 00:01:50.625
<b>which also saves them from the </b>
<b>web of this material world.</b>

17
00:01:50.625 --> 00:01:52.041
<b>Not only that,</b>

18
00:01:52.041 --> 00:01:57.833
<b>but the renunciation of these sacrifices also</b>
<b>leads to the attainment of a sweet 'nectar'.</b>

19
00:01:57.833 --> 00:02:05.000
<b>Let's understand this sweet nectar from the </b>
<b>perspective of both materialism and spirituality.</b>

20
00:02:05.000 --> 00:02:08.083
<b>At the material level, the person </b>
<b>performing the sacrifice</b>

21
00:02:08.083 --> 00:02:11.083
<b>attains self-satisfaction and prosperity.</b>

22
00:02:11.083 --> 00:02:15.958
<b>However, far sweeter than this is the </b>
<b>spiritual 'nectar' of these sacrifices,</b>

23
00:02:15.958 --> 00:02:19.541
<b>which is to come closer to the Supreme Lord.</b>

24
00:02:19.541 --> 00:02:24.125
<b>You can think of the Supreme Lord </b>
<b>as a great ocean of nectar,</b>

25
00:02:24.125 --> 00:02:31.458
<b>and with each sacrifice, an ascetic </b>
<b>sips that nectar drop by drop.</b>

26
00:02:31.458 --> 00:02:33.750
<b>And then, a time comes</b>

27
00:02:33.750 --> 00:02:40.083
<b>when that person merges into the Supreme </b>
<b>Lord Himself, into that infinite ocean of nectar.</b>

28
00:02:40.083 --> 00:02:43.833
<b>Lord Krishna calls this level Brahma Sanatana.</b>

29
00:02:43.833 --> 00:02:48.166
<b>And reaching this level of Brahman</b>
<b> is true liberation.</b>

30
00:02:48.166 --> 00:02:49.000
<b>Ultimately,</b>

31
00:02:49.000 --> 00:02:52.833
<b>through this verse, Lord Krishna wants to convey</b>

32
00:02:52.833 --> 00:02:55.750
<b>that the form of these sacrifices may be different,</b>

33
00:02:55.750 --> 00:02:58.333
<b>the renunciations given may be different —</b>

34
00:02:58.333 --> 00:02:59.166
<b>but</b>

35
00:02:59.166 --> 00:03:02.083
<b>the final objectives of all of them are the same —</b>

36
00:03:02.083 --> 00:03:05.041
<b>purification and liberation.</b>

37
00:03:05.041 --> 00:03:07.625
<b>And it is extremely important to understand this</b>

38
00:03:07.625 --> 00:03:12.750
<b>because the methods or practices described </b>
<b>in the Vedas and scriptures,</b>

39
00:03:12.750 --> 00:03:15.250
<b>which many people have considered different,</b>

40
00:03:15.250 --> 00:03:18.166
<b>are not fundamentally so different</b>

41
00:03:18.166 --> 00:03:24.416
<b>because the ultimate goal of all </b>
<b>of them is spiritual liberation.</b>

42
00:03:29.208 --> 00:03:32.625
<b>When you clean your house</b>

43
00:03:32.625 --> 00:03:37.083
<b>or organize everything at your workplace,</b>

44
00:03:37.083 --> 00:03:45.083
<b>the purpose may be to make your </b>
<b>home or workplace attractive.</b>

45
00:03:45.083 --> 00:03:46.625
<b>Similarly,</b>

46
00:03:46.625 --> 00:03:52.708
<b>one purpose of sacrifice is to </b>
<b>cleanse and purify the mind,</b>

47
00:03:52.708 --> 00:03:56.750
<b>to make the mind attractive.</b>

48
00:03:56.750 --> 00:04:00.958
<b>Some people donate for this, some observe fasts,</b>

49
00:04:00.958 --> 00:04:05.625
<b>some follow strict physical and mental discipline,</b>

50
00:04:05.625 --> 00:04:11.541
<b>and some spend time in spiritual </b>
<b>knowledge and yoga.</b>

51
00:04:11.541 --> 00:04:19.458
<b>But through cleaning the house or workplace, </b>
<b>you also achieve many deeper purposes.</b>

52
00:04:19.458 --> 00:04:21.375
<b>For example,</b>

53
00:04:21.375 --> 00:04:25.000
<b>a clean house gives satisfaction,</b>

54
00:04:25.000 --> 00:04:30.666
<b>and when you organize scattered</b>
<b>things at the workplace,</b>

55
00:04:30.666 --> 00:04:35.166
<b>you are reducing distracting objects,</b>

56
00:04:35.166 --> 00:04:41.541
<b>which increases your concentration </b>
<b>and clarifies your thoughts.</b>

57
00:04:41.541 --> 00:04:43.291
<b>In the same way,</b>

58
00:04:43.291 --> 00:04:48.833
<b>the purpose of sacrifice does not stop</b>
<b>at cleansing and purifying the mind;</b>

59
00:04:48.833 --> 00:04:52.625
<b>it also has many deeper purposes.</b>

60
00:04:52.625 --> 00:04:56.208
<b>The supreme level of sacrifice is</b>

61
00:04:56.208 --> 00:04:59.083
<b>Brahma Sanatana,</b>

62
00:04:59.083 --> 00:05:00.375
<b>that is,</b>

63
00:05:00.375 --> 00:05:03.583
<b>the realization of the eternal Brahman,</b>

64
00:05:03.583 --> 00:05:08.541
<b>which is a completely spiritual experience.</b>

65
00:05:08.541 --> 00:05:12.791
<b>Always remember this supreme objective.</b>

66
00:05:12.791 --> 00:05:19.708
<b>Never underestimate any of your </b>
<b>renunciations or sacrifices.</b>

67
00:05:19.708 --> 00:05:23.500
<b>Ponder upon this.</b>

68
00:05:28.416 --> 00:05:30.583
<b>The spirit of sacrifice.</b>

69
00:05:30.583 --> 00:05:33.250
<b>That is yajna.</b>

70
00:05:33.250 --> 00:05:40.666
<b>And in a family, this feeling makes </b>
<b>relationships even sweeter.</b>

71
00:05:40.666 --> 00:05:42.166
<b>Imagine</b>

72
00:05:42.166 --> 00:05:45.333
<b>a family where every member</b>

73
00:05:45.333 --> 00:05:49.333
<b>doesn't hesitate to give up a little of their time,</b>

74
00:05:49.333 --> 00:05:54.500
<b>convenience and preferences for the </b>
<b>good of others</b>

75
00:05:54.500 --> 00:05:58.125
<b>but considers it their privilege.</b>

76
00:05:58.125 --> 00:06:00.000
<b>In such a family,</b>

77
00:06:00.000 --> 00:06:04.875
<b>the roots of love and respect will be so deep</b>

78
00:06:04.875 --> 00:06:12.541
<b>that no difficult situation will be </b>
<b>able to shake this family tree.</b>

79
00:06:12.541 --> 00:06:17.625
<b>Just as water is necessary to keep plants alive,</b>

80
00:06:17.625 --> 00:06:18.750
<b>similarly,</b>

81
00:06:18.750 --> 00:06:26.416
<b>selfless love and sacrifice are necessary </b>
<b>for relationships to flourish.</b>

82
00:06:26.416 --> 00:06:32.250
<b>True love only grows by sharing.</b>

83
00:06:32.250 --> 00:06:34.708
<b>Ponder upon this.</b>

84
00:06:39.500 --> 00:06:45.916
<b>The renunciation of sacrifice leads to </b>
<b>the attainment of spiritual nectar.</b>

85
00:06:45.916 --> 00:06:52.291
<b>And this is fully applicable in the </b>
<b>professional context as well.</b>

86
00:06:52.291 --> 00:06:58.583
<b>In the professional environment too, </b>
<b>a person makes many kinds of sacrifices, </b>

87
00:06:58.583 --> 00:07:04.375
<b>gives their time, gives their skills, </b>
<b>gives their experience.</b>

88
00:07:04.375 --> 00:07:05.750
<b>Now imagine,</b>

89
00:07:05.750 --> 00:07:09.583
<b>if only personal interest is removed from this</b>

90
00:07:09.583 --> 00:07:13.208
<b>and the feeling of helping others is added,</b>

91
00:07:13.208 --> 00:07:16.375
<b>how beautiful the situation would become.</b>

92
00:07:16.375 --> 00:07:23.500
<b>An organization where all colleagues </b>
<b>are driven by only one purpose,</b>

93
00:07:23.500 --> 00:07:27.833
<b>for which they do not shy </b>
<b>away from helping others.</b>

94
00:07:27.833 --> 00:07:31.541
<b>Everyone openly lends a hand to each other.</b>

95
00:07:31.541 --> 00:07:39.250
<b>For others, they dedicate, they </b>
<b>sacrifice their time and skills.</b>

96
00:07:39.250 --> 00:07:45.333
<b>These sacrifices made selflessly</b>
<b>also make it a yajna.</b>

97
00:07:45.333 --> 00:07:51.750
<b>And if you are a senior official appointed </b>
<b>to a leadership position,</b>

98
00:07:51.750 --> 00:07:58.666
<b>then to create such an environment, you </b>
<b>will have to adopt this spirit yourself.</b>

99
00:07:58.666 --> 00:08:03.125
<b>Selflessly, you will have to become instrumental </b>
<b>in the progress of others.</b>

100
00:08:03.125 --> 00:08:09.291
<b>You will have to make the sacrifice of </b>
<b>dedicating your time and experience for them.</b>

101
00:08:09.291 --> 00:08:15.333
<b>Adopt the spirit of yajna towards the </b>
<b>organization and your colleagues.</b>

